  "content": {
    "id": "p8-q21-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Prove that $\\cos 3\\theta=4\\cos^{3}\\theta-3\\cos\\theta$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\cos 3\\theta=4\\cos^{3}\\theta-3\\cos\\theta$.\n\nExpand $\\cos(2\\theta+\\theta)$, apply the double-angle formulas, then use $\\sin^{2}\\theta=1-\\cos^{2}\\theta$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\cos 3\\theta&=\\cos(2\\theta+\\theta)\\\\\\cos 3\\theta&=\\cos 2\\theta\\cos\\theta-\\sin 2\\theta\\sin\\theta\\\\\\cos 3\\theta&=(1-2\\sin^{2}\\theta)\\cos\\theta-(2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta)\\sin\\theta\\\\\\cos 3\\theta&=\\cos\\theta-2\\sin^{2}\\theta\\cos\\theta-2\\sin^{2}\\theta\\cos\\theta\\\\\\cos 3\\theta&=\\cos\\theta-4\\sin^{2}\\theta\\cos\\theta\\\\\\cos 3\\theta&=\\cos\\theta-4(1-\\cos^{2}\\theta)\\cos\\theta\\\\\\cos 3\\theta&=4\\cos^{3}\\theta-3\\cos\\theta.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 64
  },
